## Findings

- **P1 — Partial scopes discard required boundary inputs.** [`scheduler.py:415`](D:/@Workspace/@Development/@Scripts/@Python/ScriptToScene-Studio-V2/studio/workflows/scheduler.py:415) removes every edge whose source falls outside the calculated scope, then [`scheduler.py:456`](D:/@Workspace/@Development/@Scripts/@Python/ScriptToScene-Studio-V2/studio/workflows/scheduler.py:456) resolves inputs only from the reduced graph. Consequently, `from_node`, `retry_failed`, and `retry_failed_desc` invoke their starting node without its upstream data; diamond descendants also lose inputs from branches outside the scope. An adversarial TTS case reported `succeeded` while receiving `{}` instead of its required script. Boundary inputs must be restored from verified cache entries, or upstream nodes must remain cache-only dependencies with required-port validation enforced before invocation.

- **P1 — Real UI reruns cannot reuse the project-scoped cache.** Cache keys include `project_id` at [`cache.py:143`](D:/@Workspace/@Development/@Scripts/@Python/ScriptToScene-Studio-V2/studio/workflows/cache.py:143), but the frontend request at [`workflow.js:283`](D:/@Workspace/@Development/@Scripts/@Python/ScriptToScene-Studio-V2/frontend/src/features/workflow/stores/workflow.js:283) sends no project ID. For normal `project.setup` workflows, the backend therefore generates a fresh ID every time at [`execution.py:102`](D:/@Workspace/@Development/@Scripts/@Python/ScriptToScene-Studio-V2/studio/workflows/execution.py:102). Thus an unchanged Full Video rerun executes everything, and a history retry cannot preserve successful cached work. Rerun/retry actions need to submit the inspected execution’s project ID, or use another stable project identity.

- **P1 — Managed music references bypass cache integrity checks.** [`music.py:44`](D:/@Workspace/@Development/@Scripts/@Python/ScriptToScene-Studio-V2/studio/workflows/adapters/music.py:44) returns a managed track URL but deliberately sets `artifact_refs` to an empty list at [`music.py:52`](D:/@Workspace/@Development/@Scripts/@Python/ScriptToScene-Studio-V2/studio/workflows/adapters/music.py:52). Cache lookup consequently validates no file at [`cache.py:172`](D:/@Workspace/@Development/@Scripts/@Python/ScriptToScene-Studio-Studio-V2/studio/workflows/cache.py:172), so a deleted or replaced track remains a cache hit. The cache integrity layer needs support for approved managed-media roots, including the music library.

- **P2 — `retry_failed` has no failed execution to retry.** Scope calculation treats the mode as merely “run this target” at [`scheduler.py:330`](D:/@Workspace/@Development/@Scripts/@Python/ScriptToScene-Studio-V2/studio/workflows/scheduler.py:330). The API receives neither a source execution ID nor verifies that the node failed; only the UI performs a transient status check before calling [`ExecutionPanel.vue:121`](D:/@Workspace/@Development/@Scripts/@Python/ScriptToScene-Studio-V2/frontend/src/features/workflow/components/ExecutionPanel.vue:121). Any node can therefore be submitted as `retry_failed`, and the backend cannot bind the retry to prior inputs, project, fingerprints, or failure state.

- **P2 — “Expand JSON” expands an irreversible summary, not the recorded value.** Execution records store only `resolved_inputs_summary` and `outputs_summary` at [`models.py:25`](D:/@Workspace/@Development/@Scripts/@Python/ScriptToScene-Studio-V2/studio/workflows/models.py:25). `_summarize` replaces strings with character counts and truncates collections at [`scheduler.py:185`](D:/@Workspace/@Development/@Scripts/@Python/ScriptToScene-Studio-V2/studio/workflows/scheduler.py:185). The history UI then labels that lossy object “Expand JSON” at [`ExecutionPanel.vue:266`](D:/@Workspace/@Development/@Scripts/@Python/ScriptToScene-Studio-V2/frontend/src/features/workflow/components/ExecutionPanel.vue:266). A failed run cannot be deeply inspected as required; redacted full values or a bounded, separately retrievable detail payload are needed.

All committed checks pass: 121 backend tests plus 38 subtests, 84 frontend tests, and the production build. No review changes were made. I left concurrent uncommitted changes under `_dev/loop-engineering/` untouched.
